restore.description:
Old: {old}

New: {new}

Journal status: {status}

Restores original IDs and settings for both bulbs, including enabled state. Later edits to those settings are overwritten. History and external changes are not restored.

For Zigbee copying, newly added bindings and memberships are also removed. Entries present before replacement are preserved. The selected backend and affected devices must be available. For Zigbee2MQTT, MQTT must be connected to the original bridge. Undo does not restore reporting changes or coordinator bindings automatically configured by Zigbee2MQTT.

confirm_zha.description:
**{old} → {archived}** (name: {name}_OLD, disabled).

**{new} → {old}** (name: {name}). Area ID: {area}. Area, labels, aliases and custom icon are copied.

**Resolve before replacing:** {blockers}

**Different light capabilities:** {capabilities} (`capabilities` means different color/dimming/effect support). Review scenes.

Take a Home Assistant backup. References to the original entity ID will target the new bulb. History is not migrated. Clean up references to the new bulb’s previous ID manually. External systems and dynamic templates cannot be verified here. Hardware device IDs and unique IDs stay unchanged. Pause affected automations during replacement; state changes will occur.

