This preview uses Zigbee2MQTT's cached records, not a live read of device binding tables. Explicitly accept this limitation before copying. Each write requires a matching bridge response and updated bridge records. This does not independently verify the device's binding table.

Original entries are retained. Undo removes the requested entries added by the wizard and preserves entries already recorded on the new bulb. Zigbee2MQTT may also configure reporting or coordinator bindings as a side effect of its normal bind/group commands; those side effects are not undone. On-device Zigbee scenes are not copied. Wake battery remotes and keep the old bulb registered for recovery.
